# StratForge platform secrets -- NAMES ONLY.
#
# This file is committed. It documents which platform secrets a deployment
# needs; it must never contain a value, not even a placeholder that looks
# real. Real values live outside the repository, one file per environment:
#
#   $STRATFORGE_SECRETS_DIR/development.env
#   $STRATFORGE_SECRETS_DIR/canary.env
#   $STRATFORGE_SECRETS_DIR/production.env
#
# with mode 0600 on POSIX. Canary and Production never share a file, so one
# cannot read the other's credentials. If STRATFORGE_SECRETS_DIR is unset the
# default is %PROGRAMDATA%\StratForge\secrets on Windows and
# /etc/stratforge/secrets elsewhere. A directory inside this repository is
# refused outright.
#
# These are platform secrets: credentials the deployment owns. A user's own
# AI provider key is NOT one of these -- it belongs to their workspace, is
# encrypted at rest and is never returned to any client.

NTA_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
NTA_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
NTA_RESEND_API_KEY=
NTA_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
STRATFORGE_OWNER_MARKET_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
STRATFORGE_CONNECTOR_RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY=
